    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0459" n="1193" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1193"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Muruaga to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In confirmation of his last communication of March 20 last, the undersigned,
                    envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of Spain, has the honor to
                    notify the honorable Secretary of State that, according to official and reliable
                    information, a filibustering expedition, commanded by Gonzalo de Quesada,
                    secretary of the Cuban Revolutionary Junta, and a naturalized American citizen,
                    is on the point of setting out from Tampa, Fla., for the Island of Cuba.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. de Muruaga.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
